{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SwiftRouting"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Navigation Basics","role":"article"},"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/RouterModel","doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/BaseRouterModel","doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/BaseRouter","doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/PresentationModel"],"generated":true,"title":"Navigation","anchor":"Navigation"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/Router"},{"type":"text","text":" is your primary interface for programmatic navigation. Every "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/RoutingView"},{"type":"text","text":" creates its own router, accessible via the SwiftUI environment."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Accessing-the-Router","text":"Accessing the Router","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use the ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Environment","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property wrapper to access the router:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct MyView: View {","    @Environment(\\.router) private var router","    ","    var body: some View {","        Button(\"Navigate\") {","            router.push(HomeRoute.detail(id: 42))","        }","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Push-Navigation","text":"Push Navigation","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Push adds a route to the navigation stack with a standard slide animation:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/\/ Push a new route","router.push(HomeRoute.detail(id: 42))","","\/\/ Using NavigationLink","NavigationLink(route: HomeRoute.detail(i